{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1058357-what-s-the-role-of-the-ordo-dracul","id":1058357,"title":"What's the role of the Ordo Dracul","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-05T04:28:00-08:00","id":1058357,"title":"What's the role of the Ordo Dracul","content":"So, question time.<br /> <br /> I've been messing around with some Vampire settings of late, thinking of trying some new directions with the game than my usual things. Back with Blood and Smoke first came out, I remember talk about how each of the covenants had reasons to have rivals stick around. Each covenant kind of fitting into its own niche, having its own specialties.<br /> <br /> The Invictus specialize in keeping the Masquerade quiet through organization manipulations and raising the best Retainers (even if the PC is that retainer!). Notories who bond their cotories and ghouls can grant them some pretty powerful abilities.<br /> The Carthians have an entire &quot;shrug off outside influence&quot; vibe going on with them with their Law, and make everyone like them with lawyer speak. They are awesome at upholding the law, no matter what it is.<br /> The Lancea et Sanctum has the whole Lore Keeper vibe going on with their Libraries as well as a lot of witch hunter abilities and &quot;sanctuary.&quot; Even Theban lends itself to the latter two. Very handy to have. Theban actually lends itself to making awesome sheriffs, in my not-actually-humble opinion.<br /> The Circle of the Crone has the best &quot;witches&quot; - especially for diviners and other mystical paths, like summoning, dealing with ghosts, etc.<br /> <br /> Each of these kind of fit well into a society, and gives reasons why you'd want to keep each of them around in your domain. Need the future foretold, go to an Acolyte. Have someoen that needs to be tracked down and judged? Lance, you're up. Carthians, for all their trouble causing, make excellent aids and will follow the Law, because that's their strength. Invictus make everyone around them better.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm sure that some people will agree or disagree with the above. Maybe you'll have different takes, maybe you'll have different wants. Its the general direction I'm taking my city in. But, here's the cornerstone of where I'm drawing a giant &quot;???&quot; over my head while looking at the covenants.<br /> <br /> What good is the Ordo Dracul? Seriously. Ignore Zirnitra / Ziva for now - they're both rare enough and varied enough that I don't want them to influence the covenant as a whole in my city. So, what do these Dragons do for the city at large? What social role do they fill? What niche do they claim beyond &quot;be the best vampire you can be?&quot; Asendant could be good for &quot;daylight vampires,&quot; but that's literally what most other covenants use ghouls for. I'm at a loss on how the Ordo Dracul would really contribute to vampire society as a whole here, as I'm looking at for my game.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, I know that the Ordo Dracul are technically supposed to be secret society. Never seen them run that way, but there you are. So not having a role in society might be a thing. But they don't really lend themselves to being a hidden society within Vampire ranks either. They just seem to be... there. Maybe just really good Elysium Keepers, given all the Wyrm Nest merits? I was kind of hoping for something pulled from the core book, but they're just short on ideas imho.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, does anyone have any other ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-05-2017, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T04:45:04-08:00","id":1058360,"title":"","content":"They are the Lore Keepers for supernatural stuff. They specifically go out to supernatural places and spend their time studying them to find out how it works, which they called Wyrm Nests iirc. If you're looking for a way to get into the underworld, ask the Ordo Dracul and they might tell how to open a nearby avernian gate for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T04:49:58-08:00","id":1058362,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't that be the Circle? They specialize in Occult, they have rituals that deal with ghosts, they have divinations that can point you in the direction of a doorway, they can probably have a ritual to open said dooorway....<br /> <br /> Heck, even the Circle's predasessor in Dark Era's London specialized in supernatural contacts before they got into Cruac.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-05-2017, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T06:09:11-08:00","id":1058377,"title":"","content":"You would have to change how the Ordo Dracul operates if you want them to &quot;beneficially&quot; contribute to vampire society because as it is is now, they don't provide a public product or service. Their entire purpose is to alter the &quot;physics&quot; of vampiric existence to make themselves better than everyone else. Supposedly to overthrow God but more realistically to just become the top of the local heap. If they shared the fruits of their discoveries you could classify them as innovators but whenever they discover something they proceed to conceal it even from each other. Either that or you need to manufacture a threat where they would, based on their ability to temporarily pervert the functions of powers (via scales) need to concoct a pseudoscientic solution. If it's a disease or infection, it would have to be ongoing treatment and not a permanent cure. (Which explains why they're kept around.) Or maybe something bizarre like collecting vitae from every clan every 15 years meeting esoteric conditions to hand over to a Gentry so the Hedge doesn't weaken. Or a Hunger Games knockoff where a fledgling or neonate from each clan is offered every year to the local werewolves (who specialize in hunting vampires) as payment for losing a territory war to them. The Ordo Dracul thinks they've perfected a &quot;vampire&quot; capable of finally winning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T06:57:16-08:00","id":1058387,"title":"","content":"Do scientists and scholars contribute anything immediate or tangible to the society? That's the usual social roll I see the Ordo occupy. How you treat them will vary depending on whether the domain's resources and infrastructure can support them, and how the Ordo conduct themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T08:17:54-08:00","id":1058413,"title":"","content":"The Ordo Dracul don't contribute at all is the point. Scientists and scholars publish their findings. The Ordo Dracul hoards their discoveries.<br /> <br /> Not only that, the other covenants are just as capable of producing scientists and researchers who are just as good as or superior to the types drawn to the Ordo Dracul thanks to their fields of interest/excellence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 03-05-2017, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T08:32:10-08:00","id":1058423,"title":"","content":"I also see them as specialist of the weird. Not everything in the Chronicles of Darkness is easily put in categories such as ghost and spirits. Sometimes you encounter things that just cant be easily classified. The Ordo Dracul with their exploratory, researchy vibe, would be well suited to offer explanation to such things. (BTW i know its not perfect, i'm sort of 'thinking out loud' to try to help).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T08:50:16-08:00","id":1058430,"title":"","content":"The Dragons are absolutely the scientists and scholars of Kindred society. They may keep their methods secret, but so do all of the other Covenants. They do, however, share the benefits of their findings. For good examples of services the Dragons can provide other Kindred, look no further than the Scales, most of which can be performed on other subjects. Epidermal Shielding Bath to help someone who needs to go out during the day. Flesh Graft Treatment for someone who got caught in a house fire. Augmented Vitae Draught and Kindred Sense Endowment to roid up the Invictus' Retainers. Blood Cleansing Ritual to help Carthians escape blood bonds to tyrannical elders. Sanguinary Invigoration on the ancient Bishop's herd so he can countinue to feed safely. Etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":".  You know youre a CofD nerd when your phone auto-corrects Epidermal to Ephemeral 03-05-2017, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T09:59:02-08:00","id":1058451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1058357-what-s-the-role-of-the-ordo-dracul?p=1058387#post1058387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do scientists and scholars contribute anything immediate or tangible to the society?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. Forensic scientists help catch criminals. Social sciences help manipulate society and the individual, such as therapy or marketing. Biochemists create medicines. And so on.<br /> <br /> None of this really applies to Ordo, of course, but scientists / scholars have immense value to human society, both in the real world and the CofD, with immediate and tangible benefits for society as a whole.`<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1058357-what-s-the-role-of-the-ordo-dracul?p=1058430#post1058430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div> Umm... so they're reinventing the wheel of stuff the other covenants can already do?<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm beginning to feel that tsuasi is right, the Ordo don't really offer anything that the other four covenants don't do just as well, if not far better, and that I'll need to change them for my game. Maitrecorbo does hit on an interesting idea, being explorers, which now that I think about it, is mentioned in passing in the Ordo Dracul blurb too. I might go in that direction. I'll need to think more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-05-2017, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T10:18:06-08:00","id":1058460,"title":"","content":"Pull back; rather than looking at what they do in society, look at what they do for individuals. Every Covenant exists as an answer to the existential question of being a Vampire - the Carthians and Invictus offer purpose amd familiarity, the Circle and Sanctified offer spiritual comfort - and the Ordo likewise does the same.<br /> <br /> The Ordo has two things to offer: control (which is terrifyingly lacking for someone Embraced) and the chance of a way out somewhere down the line. If you can't see the ready appeal of that in any domain, you aren't looking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T10:33:05-08:00","id":1058469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1058357-what-s-the-role-of-the-ordo-dracul?p=1058451#post1058451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm... so they're reinventing the wheel of stuff the other covenants can already do?</div> </div> </div> </div>No? All of the examples I gave are abilities unique to the Ordo, except maybe, arguably, Skin Graft Treatment can kind of be replicated by Night Doctor Surgery if you squint. But if you want shielding against the sun, Epidermal Shielding is your only option. If you want to continue feeding on your human Herd without spending Willpower past BP6, your only option is Sanguinary Invigoration. I think there's a Carthian Law Merit in Secrets that lets you circumvent Blood Bonds, but Blood Cleansing Ritual came first, so if anyone is re-inventing the wheel it's the Carthians.<br /> <br /> The Dragons are inventors. Engineers of the Kindred Condition, creating ways to make other Kindred's unlives easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T11:45:44-08:00","id":1058503,"title":"","content":"Nope. Cruac rituals can let you feed past BP 6 without vinculum establishment. So can Invictus oaths as liege or vassal. The Invictus and Carthians can purge vinculums. Acolytes can become immune to vinculums. <br /> Resilience downgrades aggravated damage. Nothing unique or covenant exclusive about that.<br /> Night Doctor Surgery downgrades aggravated damage to be healed as lethal without the nasty side effect of potentially being placed under a 2 stage vinculum or needing 24 hr preparation time.<br /> Go out in sunlight? Use Dominate 5 on a human. Nothing covenant exclusive about that either. Someone can even transfer that ability to someone who doesn't have Dominate via Chain of Command.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T11:48:12-08:00","id":1058505,"title":"","content":"I agree that Scales are what the Ordo would provide. And I kind of envision it as a sort of deal with the devil kind of thing, given the typically unpleasant processes and consequences. You go to them when you're desperate, which I think would be an interesting dynamic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T11:53:04-08:00","id":1058507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1058357-what-s-the-role-of-the-ordo-dracul?p=1058460#post1058460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pull back; rather than looking at what they do in society, look at what they do for individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sorry, no, that's kind of very much against what I'm trying to do right now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1058357-what-s-the-role-of-the-ordo-dracul?p=1058469#post1058469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No? All of the examples I gave are abilities unique to the Ordo</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah, no, Epidermial Shielding is the only one that is unique. Pretty much everything else exists in one form or another. I mean, hells, I count three ways for the Lance to feed their elders at minimum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T12:43:08-08:00","id":1058522,"title":"","content":"The Ordo Dracul are scholars and loremasters in a purely scientific, objective sense. In a society where all five are present, with the Invictus or Carthians in charge, they are the ones who will offer their Prince the most straightforward answers to phenomena in the CofD. The Lance and the Crone, while they explore the supernatural, are very much religious organizations with their own dogma, faith, and taboos. A Prince may want the power from a certain Wyrm's Nest, but the Lance tell them not to look beyond their mission to God, and the Crone tell them that it is a sacred place and must remain undefiled and only in service of Our Mother. The Dragons will tell them &quot;eh, yeah, with a certain arcane manipulation, we could theoretically use the Wyrm's Nest to power a devotion that makes it so that anyone present is unable to lie to you. I see no reason we can't do that with a little effort.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:17:57-08:00","id":1058535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1058357-what-s-the-role-of-the-ordo-dracul?p=1058507#post1058507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, no, Epidermial Shielding is the only one that is unique. Pretty much everything else exists in one form or another. I mean, hells, I count three ways for the Lance to feed their elders at minimum.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Feed their Elders&quot; is not the same thing as &quot;allow their Elders to continue feeding on their herds.&quot; And I mean, if your criteria is what the Covenant can provide Kindred society with that no other Covenant can provide, I have a hard time seeing any of them meeting your standards of usefulness. Carthians' niche of &quot;the guys who are good at following the law&quot; can easily be emulated with Invictus Oaths. The Invictus niche of &quot;guys who are good at keeping the Masquerade&quot; can easily be emulated by anyone with Dominate. The Lancea et Sanctum niche of... uhh... they're good at being Sheriffs, you said? That's an extremely low bar, anyone can do that.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of overlap in what each Covenant can do, so I'm really not sure what you're getting at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-05-2017, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T14:12:55-08:00","id":1058564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1058357-what-s-the-role-of-the-ordo-dracul?p=1058522#post1058522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ordo Dracul are scholars and loremasters in a purely scientific, objective sense. In a society where all five are present, with the Invictus or Carthians in charge, they are the ones who will offer their Prince the most straightforward answers to phenomena in the CofD. The Lance and the Crone, while they explore the supernatural, are very much religious organizations with their own dogma, faith, and taboos. A Prince may want the power from a certain Wyrm's Nest, but the Lance tell them not to look beyond their mission to God, and the Crone tell them that it is a sacred place and must remain undefiled and only in service of Our Mother. The Dragons will tell them &amp;quot;eh, yeah, with a certain arcane manipulation, we could theoretically use the Wyrm's Nest to power a devotion that makes it so that anyone present is unable to lie to you. I see no reason we can't do that with a little effort.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly what I had in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:12:05-08:00","id":1058629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1058357-what-s-the-role-of-the-ordo-dracul#post1058357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, question time.<br /> <br /> I've been messing around with some Vampire settings of late, thinking of trying some new directions with the game than my usual things. Back with Blood and Smoke first came out, I remember talk about how each of the covenants had reasons to have rivals stick around. Each covenant kind of fitting into its own niche, having its own specialties.<br /> <br /> The Invictus specialize in keeping the Masquerade quiet through organization manipulations and raising the best Retainers (even if the PC is that retainer!). Notories who bond their cotories and ghouls can grant them some pretty powerful abilities.<br /> The Carthians have an entire &quot;shrug off outside influence&quot; vibe going on with them with their Law, and make everyone like them with lawyer speak. They are awesome at upholding the law, no matter what it is.<br /> The Lancea et Sanctum has the whole Lore Keeper vibe going on with their Libraries as well as a lot of witch hunter abilities and &quot;sanctuary.&quot; Even Theban lends itself to the latter two. Very handy to have. Theban actually lends itself to making awesome sheriffs, in my not-actually-humble opinion.<br /> The Circle of the Crone has the best &quot;witches&quot; - especially for diviners and other mystical paths, like summoning, dealing with ghosts, etc.<br /> <br /> Each of these kind of fit well into a society, and gives reasons why you'd want to keep each of them around in your domain. Need the future foretold, go to an Acolyte. Have someoen that needs to be tracked down and judged? Lance, you're up. Carthians, for all their trouble causing, make excellent aids and will follow the Law, because that's their strength. Invictus make everyone around them better.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm sure that some people will agree or disagree with the above. Maybe you'll have different takes, maybe you'll have different wants. Its the general direction I'm taking my city in. But, here's the cornerstone of where I'm drawing a giant &quot;???&quot; over my head while looking at the covenants.<br /> <br /> What good is the Ordo Dracul? Seriously. Ignore Zirnitra / Ziva for now - they're both rare enough and varied enough that I don't want them to influence the covenant as a whole in my city. So, what do these Dragons do for the city at large? What social role do they fill? What niche do they claim beyond &quot;be the best vampire you can be?&quot; Asendant could be good for &quot;daylight vampires,&quot; but that's literally what most other covenants use ghouls for. I'm at a loss on how the Ordo Dracul would really contribute to vampire society as a whole here, as I'm looking at for my game.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, I know that the Ordo Dracul are technically supposed to be secret society. Never seen them run that way, but there you are. So not having a role in society might be a thing. But they don't really lend themselves to being a hidden society within Vampire ranks either. They just seem to be... there. Maybe just really good Elysium Keepers, given all the Wyrm Nest merits? I was kind of hoping for something pulled from the core book, but they're just short on ideas imho.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, does anyone have any other ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly, you should ask yourself what rite does OD use in your Chronicle/City and in which year do you play, because for the most of it's history in most of the places Ordo Dracul in a secret society. What role does the Freemasons have? They could be the city's most wise occultists or rather be ordinary Kindred to keep the secret. Most trusted Prince's seneschal could be the hidden Kogaion, who has the wish to overthrow the Prince. Or maybe OD is more peaceful and just want to continue their studies without inquisitor's knowledge- it's up to you.<br /> <br /> Ordo Dracul could help the city in many things, but the questions is, would they do it, since for many Academies keeping hidden is one of the most important factors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:17:47-08:00","id":1058634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1058357-what-s-the-role-of-the-ordo-dracul?p=1058535#post1058535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Feed their Elders&quot; is not the same thing as &quot;allow their Elders to continue feeding on their herds.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> No, I'm not saying that. Well, I do for one of the options. But there's a lot. I mean that Theban 4 can provide bond-free vitae, I mean that there's the Stigmata option (on both feeder and feedee), there's the merit that lets you feed on other supernaturals. There's Flock, which provides willpower to replenish what you spent to be able to feed on them again. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a lot of overlap in what each Covenant can do, so I'm really not sure what you're getting at. </div> </div> </div> This isn't a question of overlap. Nothing you said makes sense for the game as I play it. Why would a Carthian go out of house when they have a good in-house method? Why would the Lance when they have several options? Your way requires me to ignore these things, and I just can't do that. <br /> <br /> <br /> Either way, I'm done. Thank you all for your contributions, but I'm afraid that I'm not seeing anything that I can use here. Good bye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:45:22-08:00","id":1058653,"title":"","content":"Damn, I was so glad and self-satisfied after posting my answer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Anyways OD isn't easy to understand their purpose, to get to know how they think and feel. It took me few years and I managed to get it as a player not a ST. When I was a ST my OD was really generic, nothing special, really. It's good to sometimes step into someone's shoes to understand their motives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T00:43:17-08:00","id":1058815,"title":"","content":"The original question seems like a fair one to me so I will try to answer it in case anyone else has the same question. If I mapped the covenants, I would put the Invictus and Carthians on one side opposite each other and the LS and CC on the other side opposite each other with the OD in the middle. The OD is traditional and innovative. It is also occult but subtle. The other covenants have a narrow focus and a niche regarding what they do well. The OD fills the gaps. I think that can make it difficult to define them and pigeonhole them.<br /> <br /> The OD could be described as &quot;scientist vampires&quot; for lack of a better description and that means they would play the same role as scientists/inventors in our society. The OD, generally, fits roles that aren't clearly favored by another covenant or that fit multiple covenants well. There is one logical disconnect though. If the OD is an open secret society (not judging since it is clearly an option) then their knowledge should be no more secret than any other covenant. All covenants have secrets. A vampire can walk up to a LS church to ask for info so if a vampire knows where the local OD chapter house is then they should be able to get info as long as they pay a price based on the information's value.<br /> <br /> As one of the occult groups, the OD fits a special niche in between the other two occultists. For example, a vampire might own a haunted building. Destroying the ghost is the realm of the LS. Magically summoning and controlling the ghost fits the CC. Now what if the vampire wants to make a long term arrangement with the ghost to guard the building. The OD is the best place to find all the info about the ghost's anchors, banes, and bans as well as means to create conditions to manifest the ghost. Other covenants might be more likely to have part of the information, but they won't have all of it. They also won't approve of using the ghost as a guard dog. It is dangerous and probably unwise which fits the OD because dangerous and unwise is their bag. This differs from the CC which necessitates including crazy to dangerous and clearly unwise.<br /> <br /> A vampire could find the information on the ghost from the OD while drawing less suspicion. The OD would approve of using a ghost to guard the building from outsiders, requiring that they be considered insiders I'm sure. Removing material that could be used for bans and banes or protecting anchors is the OD way of dealing with the ghost. Also, if a vampire is caught trying to monopolize the site the OD is less likely to have a negative view as that is what the average OD member would be expected to do.<br /> <br /> There is a subtle difference in the manner a jack-of-all-trades handles a situation compared to a specialist doing something similar in effect. Sometimes it is better, other times not. This becomes a matter of personal taste as to when the OD can excel. The OD is a little bit of all the other covenants at once and not at all like any one other covenant. That makes sense only because of how the other covenants conflict. I think that is the long and short of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T01:22:23-08:00","id":1058823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1058357-what-s-the-role-of-the-ordo-dracul?p=1058634#post1058634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No, I'm not saying that. Well, I do for one of the options. But there's a lot. I mean that Theban 4 can provide bond-free vitae, I mean that there's the Stigmata option (on both feeder and feedee), there's the merit that lets you feed on other supernaturals. There's Flock, which provides willpower to replenish what you spent to be able to feed on them again.<br /> <br /> This isn't a question of overlap. Nothing you said makes sense for the game as I play it. Why would a Carthian go out of house when they have a good in-house method? Why would the Lance when they have several options? Your way requires me to ignore these things, and I just can't do that.<br /> <br /> Either way, I'm done. Thank you all for your contributions, but I'm afraid that I'm not seeing anything that I can use here. Good bye.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know you left, so I don't expect response, but I feel that question deserves to be answered.<br /> <br /> All the Covenants cover most of each other's bases in one way or another, yes. But, that fine, the Covenants aren't based around their abilities, they are based around themes. Also, In actual play the answer to &quot;why doesn't the Carthian go in-house?&quot; may well be that there's no NPCs in the local setting with that ability. Giving every Coventant an angle to most issues expands their utility, and allows the storyteller more thematic freedom to construct their world, which I personally feel is a far better approach for the table top roleplay environment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T02:24:55-08:00","id":1058836,"title":"","content":"I like to think about Ordo Dracul not as a covenant like all the rest, but for most of it's history it is more like a secret society or a cult. Of course in terms of the mechanics they are a covenant, but some Academies might think about themselves as a Society, Order and when asked &quot;Are you a secret covenant?&quot; would Answer NO and believed they answered truthfull. Ordo Dracul functions as a covenant after The Philadelphian Rite. Wallachian Rite makes them something similar to Iluminati or Freemasons. A Sworn of Mysteries could want to be a part of Invictus to become a Senator or be a part of the Church of Longinus (in Westminster theme), pretend or even be a Carthian etc.<br /> The roles of OD can be quite different. Not all of them are genius scientists and occultist. Kogaion and Sworn of Dying Light are, but Sworn of Axe focus more on the martial aspect and Sworn of the Mysteries on the politics. Of course the covenant as a whole is heavily focused on occultism and overcoming the curse, but not all Dragons are the same. Probably most of them know something about occultism, but not all are specialists. Those who are tend to have more knowledge about supernatural beings than the Invictus or LS, because they focus on the scientific aspect more. In some radical domains Church of Longinus might &quot;recognize&quot; many ephemeral or supernatual beings as the devil were OD likes to know for the sake of knowing. Of course the situation changes in XX, XXI century. Or maybe not? Up to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","user":"Edgar McAlister","date":". 03-06-2017, 05:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T08:27:32-08:00","id":1059013,"title":"","content":"Saying &quot;step back and look at vampires as individuals&quot; may not be the most satisfying answer, but thematically it is important to retain the individual awareness even while examining how kindred society functions and why you might have a city with all five core covenants represented.<br /> <br /> OD's main claim to fame is it makes the kindred of the city &quot;better vampires&quot;. This is a good thing when applied to allies, and it gives a set of tools that may or may not be missing in other covenants at the time. Covenants are now somewhat intentionally interchangeable--if that is not desired then you'll need to do some careful editing in your setting. <br /> <br /> The &quot;best&quot; OD member from an outside perspective would also be a member of another covenant and directly lend their strength, wisdom and experiences to supporting that covenant's goals. There are merits supporting this direction. Other benefits for having them around include as discussed a non-judgmental, secular approach to solving supernatural problems, as well several more mundane ones. <br /> <br /> Both Lancea and CC are fanatical groups. Leaning too heavily on them for help in running your city, or solving its problems, runs a risk of tipping things too far in their direction--and then you lose influence/control in favor of the cult. Wise princes will avoid that by balancing both of them and having a third, wildcard option helps keep them guessing. <br /> <br /> VtR is not really meant to be clean-cut.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T10:06:07-08:00","id":1059053,"title":"","content":"MCN, if you do ever come back to this, I'd be curious how you end up retooling the Ordo to fit what you want.<br /> <br /> Last big campaign I ran the Ordo were definitely the odd-man out. I deliberately put in some mechanics (Wyrm's Nests and Leylines became a big theme) AND put them at direct odds against the city's unaligned (Invictus v. Carthians and Circle vs. Lance are built in, so Ordo vs. Unaligned plugged what I saw as a competition gap).<br /> <br /> In the end, though, I think as has been said - The Ordo don't <i>uniquely </i>have a city-based realm of service if nothing in the Scales looks like it fits. And I think that's okay, as having a Covenant that truly focuses on the individual would actually be appealing to a lot of people. There are plenty of atheists and loners who wouldn't want to deal with religious dogma, rituals, group efforts or naked power-hierarchies.<br /> <br /> The Ordo offers what looks like an academic process of advancement that as long as you are producing results, kind of leaves you to your own devices. And you get cool powers and get rid of crappy weaknesses in the process.<br /> <br /> If I was going to redo that style of campaign, I'd probably ditch the Unaligned angle and instead go full secret society for the Ordo. Have them really function as a Mystery Cult rather than a full Covenant. Lots of secret identities, mentors in masks, etc. All Kindred have their public Covenant (the other four), but you never know who might also be with the Dragons. <br /> <br /> How does a Masquerade within a Masquerade operate? At what point does the Cult/Ordo start influencing city politics? How do the other Covenants respond to losing power when they do? Could be fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T10:42:08-08:00","id":1059068,"title":"","content":"Requiem has an interesting breakdown of covenants. Someone else said this a long time ago, but there's a kind of political &quot;quadrant&quot; you can slot them into. On the <i>y-</i>axis you have <i>traditional</i> at the top and <i>progressive </i>at the bottom; on the <i>x-</i>axis you have <i>secular </i>on the left, and <i>religious </i>on the right. The Invictus is traditional-secular; the Carthians are progressive-secular; the Lancea et Sanctum is traditional-religious; the Circle of the Crone are progressive-religious.<br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul laughs at this: they're spiritual, but they defy god; they're progressive, even meritocratic, but they're a cult of personality around a nigh mythic Wallachian warlord.<br /> <br /> If the Dragons fit anywhere, it's on an occulted <i>z-</i>axis. In Nietzschean terms, they've said no to both master and slave morality, and they're looking to become the uber-Kindred. That doesn't necessarily mean that a typical Defiant is (always) a heartless, strawman libertarian, but her goals are ultimately internal, not external.<br /> <br /> Which is all to say, I concur about the Dragons being the covenant of individualism. A Dragon doesn't care if she's useful. She can provide services to the city at large, but it's almost always transactional -- it's for the advancement of self, regardless of the consequences to others (this <i>is</i> the covenant that murders humans just to see how the dominoes fall). It's not for nothing that they're the smallest sect. They're not as obviously useful as the others, and their ideology is ultimately quite isolating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 03-06-2017, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T11:13:56-08:00","id":1059081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1058357-what-s-the-role-of-the-ordo-dracul?p=1059053#post1059053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are plenty of atheists and loners who wouldn't want to deal with religious dogma, rituals, group efforts or naked power-hierarchies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that most if not ALL Ordo Dracul believe in God existence, they just don't agree with Longinus teaching. They want to overcome the curse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1058357-what-s-the-role-of-the-ordo-dracul?p=1059053#post1059053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does a Masquerade within a Masquerade operate? At what point does the Cult/Ordo start influencing city politics? How do the other Covenants respond to losing power when they do? Could be fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really fun to run OD like a secret society, both as a player and ST. A coterie of players could be the hidden secret OD in the city or they play in other covenants and OD is a secret antagonist plotting to take over the city.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1058357-what-s-the-role-of-the-ordo-dracul?p=1059068#post1059068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not for nothing that they're the smallest sect. They're not as obviously useful as the others, and their ideology is ultimately quite isolating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure that the're the smallest sect? Of course we are talking about the main covenants- Invictus, Carthians, LS, CotC and OD. It all depends about what timeline we are talking about, but Circle of the Crone is the youngest covenant (cruac is much older than CotC-assuming it is developed from Veneficia). A coterie of vampires, who worship Celtic gods not necessary are allied to the cult of Slavic gods, Egyptian etc. In XVIII - XIX century OD easily outnumbers CotC and maybe Carthians, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","user":"Edgar McAlister","date":". 03-06-2017, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T11:37:05-08:00","id":1059092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Edgar McAlister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1058357-what-s-the-role-of-the-ordo-dracul?p=1059081#post1059081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you sure that the're the smallest sect? Of course we are talking about the main covenants- Invictus, Carthians, LS, CotC and OD. It all depends about what timeline we are talking about, but Circle of the Crone is the youngest covenant (cruac is much older than CotC-assuming it is developed from Veneficia). A coterie of vampires, who worship Celtic gods not necessary are allied to the cult of Slavic gods, Egyptian etc. In XVIII - XIX century OD easily outnumbers CotC and maybe Carthians, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like it actually says they're the smallest covenant somewhere in a book? I might be misremembering, but I've always had the impression that, all things being equal, the Dragons will tend to be the smallest covenant in a given city. Look at it this way: they're an exclusionary cult of transvampirists; they're smaller than the Carthians for the same reason there are more Democrats than Masons. Timeline is less important than niche, I'd argue (with the caveat that vampires are immortal, but vampires are also jerks). The Crone are kind of odd because, as you noted, by their nature they're difficult to count. They're ecumenical to the point of absurdity. I'd still venture that there're more Crones than Dragons, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T11:42:00-08:00","id":1059096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1058357-what-s-the-role-of-the-ordo-dracul?p=1059092#post1059092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like it actually says they're the smallest covenant somewhere in a book? I might be misremembering, but I've always had the impression that, all things being equal, the Dragons will tend to be the smallest covenant in a given city. Look at it this way: they're an exclusionary cult of transvampirists; they're smaller than the Carthians for the same reason there are more Democrats than Masons. Timeline is less important than niche, I'd argue. The Crone are kind of odd because, as you noted, by their nature they're difficult to count. They're ecumenical to the point of absurdity. I'd still venture that there're more Crones than Dragons, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've found something like this in CotC description<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of all the covenants, only the Ordo Dracul controls fewer domains. That might be because when we are running things, vampire society becomes a free-for-all. </div> </div> </div>But maybe many OD Academies don't care who control the domain, they have their research to do<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In XXI century maybe there are already more Crones than Dragons, because all the pagan cults somehow united. You have a point that there are more Democrats than Masons and the niche is really important, but the timeline is important too, because without the means of communication its was difficult to spread the Kindred ideology, since most vampires don't like nomadic life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","user":"Edgar McAlister","date":". 03-06-2017, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T12:19:20-08:00","id":1059113,"title":"","content":"I definitely don't think the Ordo Dracul is the smallest <i>Covenant</i>, so much as it rules the least amount of Domains. Most Ordo Dracul are too much to run a domain, and the Invictus are much better at it. I think the only places where the Ordo Dracul would outright seize power are Places of Power, where the Wyrm's Nests are simply too valuable to risk other covenants screwing them up. I have always run DC as being a Dragon-run city, for example, because of the occult significance of the National Mall. I might have them in control of Cairo, because of the pyramids, and probably be in contest with the Lancea et Sanctum for control of Jerusalem. They're already kind of sort of in control of Beijing, according to 2e.<br /> <br /> But most cities? They can't be bothered.<br /> <br /> At the same time, the Ordo Dracul is the only covenant that is looking for <i>worthy </i>members at all. The Invictus views all Vampires as under their law, it just takes effort and merit (and age) to <i>rise </i>within the Covenant. The Lancea et Sanctum actively proselytizes and offers purpose to the wayward neonate. The Circle of the Crone welcomes brothers and sisters into the fold to become children of the Dark Mother. The Carthians need all the help they can get. The Ordo Dracul? They don't need you. They have secrets that men would kill for, and do. You need to prove yourself to them.<br /> <br /> Not everyone can do that, necessarily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T12:28:24-08:00","id":1059118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1058357-what-s-the-role-of-the-ordo-dracul?p=1059113#post1059113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the same time, the Ordo Dracul is the only covenant that is looking for <i>worthy </i>members at all. The Invictus views all Vampires as under their law, it just takes effort and merit (and age) to <i>rise </i>within the Covenant. The Lancea et Sanctum actively proselytizes and offers purpose to the wayward neonate. The Circle of the Crone welcomes brothers and sisters into the fold to become children of the Dark Mother. The Carthians need all the help they can get. The Ordo Dracul? They don't need you. They have secrets that men would kill for, and do. You need to prove yourself to them.<br /> <br /> Not everyone can do that, necessarily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's my reasoning. They're a bit more exclusionary than the others. They also spent most of their history in hiding, if the covenant book is to be believed. That being said, the setting is ambiguous enough that they could just as easily be the <i>largest </i>covenant, but keep that fact under wraps.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T20:24:54-08:00","id":1059327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1058357-what-s-the-role-of-the-ordo-dracul?p=1058522#post1058522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ordo Dracul are scholars and loremasters in a purely scientific, objective sense. In a society where all five are present, with the Invictus or Carthians in charge, they are the ones who will offer their Prince the most straightforward answers to phenomena in the CofD. The Lance and the Crone, while they explore the supernatural, are very much religious organizations with their own dogma, faith, and taboos. A Prince may want the power from a certain Wyrm's Nest, but the Lance tell them not to look beyond their mission to God, and the Crone tell them that it is a sacred place and must remain undefiled and only in service of Our Mother. The Dragons will tell them &quot;eh, yeah, with a certain arcane manipulation, we could theoretically use the Wyrm's Nest to power a devotion that makes it so that anyone present is unable to lie to you. I see no reason we can't do that with a little effort.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So they are the Kriegers of the Vampire world...neat.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-VZLXTQmnG8\" data-code=\"-VZLXTQmnG8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/-VZLXTQmnG8/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T10:40:05-08:00","id":1059605,"title":"","content":"A group of dragons I thought about were particularly focussed on that fight club concept. They ran both private and public fights to maintain a broad range of opponents. As such, they provided one of the main forms of entertainment to their peers and an elysium of sorts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T20:40:28-07:00","id":1061716,"title":"","content":"Ordo Dracul provide an &quot;Academic Atmosphere&quot;. The only other covenant that comes close is the Lancea Sanctum, and their Libraries are far more likely to be biased towards the religious beliefs of the local vampires (whatever those may be) than objective. Of course, any organization can and will have Academics, but Ordo Dracul is the first place you should think of when you want any form of academic information involving the supernatural (and even the completely natural, though you could just go to a normal university for that).<br /> <br /> They also have a function on an organism level. Every organism needs to poke and prod their surroundings to determine if if something is Food, Fuck, Dangerous, or Tool. How do you learn something new? You poke it. Play with it. Stick it in your mouth. Try to sleep with it. Think about it. Hit it with a rock. Maybe you find out something helpful. Maybe it was dangerous and you get hurt. But at least you learned something. This is a basic thing organisms do.<br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul poke things. They poke, and poke, and poke from every angle they can think of. They do this more than any other covenant, with maybe the Crones in second place.<br /> <br /> They are also probably the most likely to have connections with other supernatural beings, simply because they are always poking at things. This is relatively minor, because all the covenants would probably like to have connections with other supernatural beings, but the Ordo Dracul just have a natural inclination to have the most contact (for better or for worse).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T22:14:05-07:00","id":1061729,"title":"","content":"Yeah. The Lancea et Sanctum are archivists but they're equally bookburners when it comes to anything that disagrees with them. And the Circle is more likely to be a word of mouth type of thing, which lends itself to the problems of the game of telephone in the longform. They even had special individuals sort of like the Kogaion who were the lorekeeper for the group.<br /> <br /> For better or worse, the Ordo Dracul apply some scientific method to the supernatural and their archives would be less cluttered by personal biases. Not fully, of course, they're still vampires and were still once human.<br /> <br /> Also, they're the only group trying to get rid of the downsides of it. Everyone else is of the 'Embrace the Suck' mindset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-13-2017, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T13:38:59-07:00","id":1061959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1058357-what-s-the-role-of-the-ordo-dracul?p=1058362#post1058362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't that be the Circle? They specialize in Occult, they have rituals that deal with ghosts, they have divinations that can point you in the direction of a doorway, they can probably have a ritual to open said dooorway....<br /> <br /> Heck, even the Circle's predasessor in Dark Era's London specialized in supernatural contacts before they got into Cruac.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would suggest they serve a very similar societal role to the Circle. They just come at it from a different direction and would most likely be quite different to deal with. Likely there's a lot of variance in personal preference when it comes to which you'd rather deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/453-megazarak","name":"MegaZarak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T19:15:01-07:00","id":1063082,"title":"","content":"This has probably been said by someone else but the way I see it, looking at it from a broad prospective and from the prospective of how it works in my games-<br /> <br /> The Invictus: the old money, the past traditions, the ones of good breeding and the so called &quot;vampire royalty&quot; and their servants. The Invictus considers itself the true heirs of the Carmilla Pact from the heyday of Imperial Rome. They serve as the primary structure for vampire society and stand as the slow changing foundation to provide something stable for vampire society.<br /> <br /> The Carthian Movement: the up starts and new money, the new kids making a name for themselves and the ones trying to affect change on vampire society. This isn't so much that they believe in democracy as it is they are the force of change against the slow moving Invictus and serve more to balance things out so as to keep vampire society up to date, they also tend to be the most easy to ascend in the social ladder.<br /> <br /> Lanceum Et Sanctum: while the Invictus may be the old traditions, the Sanctum is the reason for why. The Sanctum seeks to provide a higher calling for the kindred to keep their minds off the beast and their hunger, they coat it in rituals and ancient rights because it is something many kindred remember from their former lives, almost like a touchstone of sorts.<br /> <br /> The Circle Of The Crone: the Sanctum doesn't appeal to everyone, the circle serves to pick up the stragglers. The circle and the Sanctum fill many of the same purposes but both are important because while the Sanctum is the structured and orderly one the Circle is more flexible and chaotic. No two kindred are alike and vampires need both approaches to function.<br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul: the Ordo Dracul is dedicated to evolving the vampire race to untold heights, to ending the bane of the sun and to find new ways of channeling the beast within. Where the Sanctum and the Circle do this with rituals and ceremony the Ordo applies a more scientific, or perhaps alchemical, approach. The circle and the sanctum can keep their tomes and grimoires, the Ordo has testing and experimentation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}